This appears to be a CBP ruling about a costume blouse. Such rulings typically hold that flimsy costumes are not "wearing apparel" but festive articles under heading 9505. The description emphasizes "flimsy, loose weave, loose stitching" and a costume, which is the usual reasoning for classifying it as a festive article of 9505.90.6000 (other festive, carnival or other entertainment articles; other).

Costume items such as a "Renaissance Peasant Blouse" in these rulings are classified under 9505.90.6000, since the garment is not of a durable construction typical of ordinary apparel.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The flimsy, loosely constructed costume blouse with loose stitching is not suitable for regular apparel use, so it is classified as a festive/carnival costume article in heading 9505 rather than in Chapter 61 or 62."}
